== Lemma 2.1(d): y^2 = x^3 - n^2 x is a minimal model for every squarefree n <= 2000
  checked 1215 values of n; non-minimal models: 0

== Corollary 1.2, density: E_1 has full 2-torsion and no rational cyclic subgroup of order 4
  torsion structure of E_1(Q): [2, 2]
  x-coordinates of the nonzero 4-torsion points are the roots of [x - 1, 1; x, 1; x + 1, 1; x^2 - 2*x - 1, 1; x^2 + 1, 1; x^2 + 2*x - 1, 1]
  (the linear factors give the 2-torsion; the quadratics give the points of order 4)
  degrees of the isogenies from E_1: [1, 2, 2, 2]

== Corollary 1.2, list: squarefree n <= 150 with rank E_n(Q) >= 2
  rank >= 2 proved for n = [34, 41, 65, 137, 138, 145]
  rank <= 1 proved for every other n, except [n, lower, upper] = [[113, 0, 2]]
  Tunnell counts for n = 113: 32 and 24, so 113 is not congruent

== Example 1.3: E_6 has rank one, and x(2G) = 25/4
  rank bounds for E_6: [1, 1]
  generator G = [-3, 9], x(2G) = 25/4
  the multiples mH of H = 2G, with the primes new to each denominator:
  m = 1: x(mH) = 5^2 / 2^2, new primes [2]
  m = 2: x(mH) = 1201^2 / 140^2, new primes [5, 7]
  m = 3: x(mH) = 7776485^2 / 2639802^2, new primes [3, 11, 23, 37, 47]
  m = 4: x(mH) = 2094350404801^2 / 483435791720^2, new primes [1151, 1201, 1249]
  m = 5: x(mH) = 18428872963986767525^2 / 4433082615462019402^2, new primes [13, 17, 19, 73, 97, 139, 239, 719, 3121]

== Remark 5.2: Bremner's seven-square magic square, E = 425^2, a = -41496, b = 138600
  rows alpha = -1, 0, 1 hold the b-progressions E + alpha a + beta b, beta = -1, 0, 1:
    [83521, 222121, 360721]  squares: [1, 0, 0]
    [42025, 180625, 319225]  squares: [1, 1, 1]
    [529, 139129, 277729]  squares: [1, 1, 1]
  sqf(b) = 154, rank bounds [2, 2]
  sqf(a) = 10374, rank bounds [1, 1]

== Remark 5.5: Lemma 3.1 on the rank-one curves E_n with squarefree n <= 400
  rank proved to be one, with a generator found, for 116 curves
  rank proved to be one, but no generator found, for n = [157, 173, 263, 269, 277, 293, 311, 367, 373, 389]
  rank not decided for 2 curves
  progressions found: 0; terms B_m(H), 2 <= m <= 16, without a primitive divisor: 0
